{
  "$comment": "Special votes as a share of each electorate’s total votes, by cycle. Generated by scripts/build-special-vote-shares.mjs; do not hand-edit. A seat’s share moves with the cycle, so the baseline stores each seat’s share relative to its cycle’s nationalShare and the model scales it by the live cycle’s own figure.",
  "provenance": {
    "specialVotes": "Electoral Commission, “Party Special Declaration Votes by Electorate” (electionresults.govt.nz/electionresults_{YEAR}/statistics/party-sdv-by-electorate.html), column “Total Party Special Votes Cast”. The live hosts refuse /statistics/*.html, so the table is read through the Wayback Machine.",
    "votes": "The same cycle’s archive XML: each seat’s e{NN}.xml total_votes_cast, which is the seat’s final count with specials included — the basis the live feed publishes and the model divides by.",
    "note": "2023 reconciles to 602,488 of 2,884,111 named electorates against the Commission’s published 603,257 of 2,883,412; 2020 to 504,621 against 504,625. The residual is electorates the table lists but the XML does not name."
